{% load advisory_tags %}
{% comment %}
The vulnerabilities panel's toolbar, table and footer: one page of findings.

Everything here is resolved on the server. A component can carry thousands of
findings, and rendering them all to show five cost 5.1s and 8.5MB of HTML on the
largest one we have seen, so the table holds one page and the filters run before
the slice rather than after it.

The whole region swaps as one, because the toolbar carries state the table shows
(the result count, which severities are on offer) and the two must never
disagree. The card around it is not re-rendered, so the panel stays open.

Every control is a real form field or a real link, and the endpoint they point
at redirects a non-HTMX request to the component page carrying the same
parameters. So the panel filters and pages with JavaScript off, and no control
needs a second URL for that case.

That same property is what makes hx-push-url safe below: every swap would
otherwise leave the address bar on the component page's bare URL, so a refresh,
a Back, or a link sent to a colleague would drop the filters and the page. What
gets pushed is a URL the server already renders on its own.
{% endcomment %}
<div id="component-vulnerabilities-table">
    <c-tables.shell nested>
    <form method="get"
          action="{{ vuln_panel_url }}"
          hx-get="{{ vuln_panel_url }}"
          hx-target="#component-vulnerabilities-table"
          hx-swap="outerHTML"
          hx-push-url="true"
          hx-trigger="change, input changed delay:350ms from:#vuln-search, submit">
        {% comment %}
        The marker that tells the view this request came from the form. Without
        it an unticked checkbox and an untouched page are the same request, and
        the view cannot tell "hide suppressed rows" from "nobody has said".
        {% endcomment %}
        <input type="hidden" name="vuln_submitted" value="1">
        <c-tables.toolbar class="[&>div:first-child]:flex-wrap">
        {% comment %}
        hx-preserve keeps the live input across the swap, so a search that fires
        mid-word does not move the cursor back to the start.
        {% endcomment %}
        <c-tables.search id="vuln-search" label="Search vulnerabilities" placeholder="Search vulnerabilities..." class="max-w-xs" name="vuln_search" value="{{ vuln_panel.query.search }}" hx-preserve="true" />
        <c-tables.select id="vuln-sev-filter" label="Filter by severity" name="vuln_severity">
        <option value="all">All Severities</option>
        {% for severity in vuln_panel.severity_options %}
            <option value="{{ severity }}"
                    {% if severity == vuln_panel.query.severity %}selected{% endif %}>{{ severity|capfirst }}</option>
        {% endfor %}
        </c-tables.select>
        <c-tables.select id="vuln-state-filter" label="Filter by VEX analysis state" name="vuln_state">
        <option value="all">All States</option>
        {% for state in vuln_panel.state_options %}
            <option value="{{ state.value }}"
                    {% if state.value == vuln_panel.query.state %}selected{% endif %}>{{ state.label }}</option>
        {% endfor %}
        </c-tables.select>
        {% if vuln_panel.kev_total %}
            <c-forms.checkbox name="vuln_kev" :checked="vuln_panel.query.kev_only">Known exploited ({{ vuln_panel.kev_total }})</c-forms.checkbox>
        {% endif %}
        <c-tables.select id="vuln-per-page" label="Rows per page" name="vuln_per_page">
        {% for size in vuln_panel.per_page_choices %}
            <option value="{{ size }}"
                    {% if size == vuln_panel.per_page %}selected{% endif %}>{{ size }} per page</option>
        {% endfor %}
        </c-tables.select>
        {% comment %}
        Suppressed rows show by default, struck through and labelled with the
        state that cleared them; the toggle hides them so the working list
        matches the open counts. Picking a suppressing state in the filter
        implies showing them, so the two controls cannot ask for nothing.
        {% endcomment %}
        {% if vuln_panel.suppressed_total %}
            <c-forms.checkbox class="whitespace-nowrap" name="vuln_suppressed" :checked="vuln_panel.query.show_suppressed">
            Show suppressed ({{ vuln_panel.suppressed_total }})
            </c-forms.checkbox>
        {% endif %}
        <noscript>
            <c-buttons.secondary size="sm" type="submit">Apply</c-buttons.secondary>
        </noscript>
        </c-tables.toolbar>
    </form>
    <c-tables.table>
    <c-tables.head>
    <c-tables.header-cell>Severity</c-tables.header-cell>
    <c-tables.header-cell nowrap>Advisory</c-tables.header-cell>
    <c-tables.header-cell>Package</c-tables.header-cell>
    <c-tables.header-cell>Fixed in</c-tables.header-cell>
    <c-tables.header-cell>Status</c-tables.header-cell>
    {% if can_triage %}<c-tables.header-cell nowrap>Triage</c-tables.header-cell>{% endif %}
    </c-tables.head>
    <tbody>
        {% for vuln in vuln_panel.rows %}
            <c-tables.row>
            <c-tables.cell nowrap>
            {% if vuln.severity == 'critical' or vuln.severity == 'high' or vuln.severity == 'medium' or vuln.severity == 'low' %}
                <c-badges.severity level="{{ vuln.severity|lower }}" class="
                {% if vuln.vex_suppressed %}line-through{% endif %}
                ">
                {{ vuln.severity|capfirst }}
                </c-badges.severity>
            {% else %}
                <c-badges.severity level="unknown" class="
                {% if vuln.vex_suppressed %}line-through{% endif %}
                ">
                {{ vuln.severity|title }}
                </c-badges.severity>
            {% endif %}
            </c-tables.cell>
            <c-tables.cell nowrap>
            {% with vuln_url=vuln.id|advisory_url %}
                {% if vuln_url %}
                    <a href="{{ vuln_url }}"
                       target="_blank"
                       rel="noopener"
                       class="font-medium text-primary hover:underline inline-flex items-center gap-1">
                        {{ vuln.id }}<i class="fas fa-external-link-alt text-[0.65rem]"></i>
                    </a>
                {% else %}
                    <span class="font-medium text-text-muted">{{ vuln.id }}</span>
                {% endif %}
            {% endwith %}
            {% if vuln.kev %}
                <c-badges.solid-danger size="sm" class="ml-1.5 align-middle" title="In CISA's Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog">KEV</c-badges.solid-danger>
            {% endif %}
            {% if vuln.aliases %}<div class="text-xs text-text-muted mt-1">Aliases: {{ vuln.aliases|join:", " }}</div>{% endif %}
            </c-tables.cell>
            <c-tables.cell>
            <span class="font-medium text-text">{{ vuln.package }}</span>
            {% if vuln.version %}<span class="text-text-muted">· {{ vuln.version }}</span>{% endif %}
            {% if vuln.ecosystem %}<c-badges.secondary class="ml-2">{{ vuln.ecosystem }}</c-badges.secondary>{% endif %}
            </c-tables.cell>
            <c-tables.cell>
            {% if vuln.fixed %}
                <span class="font-mono text-sm text-success">{{ vuln.fixed }}</span>
            {% else %}
                <span class="text-text-muted">Not reported</span>
            {% endif %}
            </c-tables.cell>
            <c-tables.cell>
            {% if vuln.vex_suppressed %}
                <span class="text-info">
                    {% if vuln.vex_state == 'false_positive' %}
                        False positive
                    {% elif vuln.vex_state == 'resolved' %}
                        Fixed
                    {% else %}
                        Not affected
                    {% endif %}
                    ·
                    {% if vuln.vex_manual %}
                        manually
                    {% else %}
                        VEX
                    {% endif %}
                </span>
                {% if vuln.vex_justification %}
                    <div class="text-xs text-text-muted mt-1">{{ vuln.vex_justification_label }}</div>
                {% endif %}
            {% elif vuln.vex_state == 'in_triage' %}
                <span class="text-warning">Under investigation</span>
            {% else %}
                <span class="text-text-muted">Affected</span>
            {% endif %}
            </c-tables.cell>
            {% if can_triage %}
                <c-tables.cell nowrap>
                {% comment %}Same event and the same payload the assessment card
                dispatches, so one modal serves both and a decision made here
                reads identically to one made there. The purl anchors it to the
                package; without one the modal falls back to component scope.{% endcomment %}
                <c-buttons.outline size="sm" @click="$dispatch('open-triage', { id: '{{ vuln.id|escapejs }}', purl: '{{ vuln.purl|default:''|escapejs }}', state: '{{ vuln.vex_state|default:''|escapejs }}', justification: '{{ vuln.vex_justification|default:''|escapejs }}', detail: '{{ vuln.vex_detail|default:''|escapejs }}', aliases: '{{ vuln.aliases|default:''|join:','|escapejs }}' })">
                <i class="fas fa-stethoscope mr-1"></i>Triage
                </c-buttons.outline>
                </c-tables.cell>
            {% endif %}
            </c-tables.row>
        {% empty %}
            <tr>
                <td colspan="{% if can_triage %}6{% else %}5{% endif %}"
                    class="text-center">
                    <span class="text-text-muted">No vulnerabilities match your search.</span>
                </td>
            </tr>
        {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
    </c-tables.table>
    {# Footer: row count + full report on the left, pagination on the right #}
    <c-tables.footer>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
        <c-tables.info>
        Showing {{ vuln_panel.start_index }} to {{ vuln_panel.end_index }} of {{ vuln_panel.total }}
        {% if not vuln_panel.suppressed_shown and vuln_panel.suppressed_total %}
            · {{ vuln_panel.suppressed_total }} suppressed hidden
        {% endif %}
        </c-tables.info>
        {% if latest_vuln_sbom_id %}
            <a href="{% url 'sboms:sbom_vulnerabilities' latest_vuln_sbom_id %}"
               class="text-sm text-primary hover:underline no-underline inline-flex items-center gap-1">
                View full scan report<i class="fas fa-arrow-right text-xs"></i>
            </a>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
    {% comment %}
    hx-boost turns these two links into panel swaps and leaves them as ordinary
    links when it is not running. Scoped to the pager rather than the region, so
    the full-report link above still navigates.

    hx-push-url is off because boosting pushes by default, and the address bar
    would then hold the panel endpoint rather than the page the reader is on.
    The links still point at that endpoint, which redirects a plain visit back to
    the page, so the no-JS path is unaffected.
    {% endcomment %}
    {% if vuln_panel.page_count > 1 %}
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2"
             hx-boost="true"
             hx-push-url="false"
             hx-target="#component-vulnerabilities-table"
             hx-swap="outerHTML">
            {% if vuln_panel.has_prev %}
                <c-buttons.secondary size="sm" aria-label="Previous page" href="{{ vuln_prev_url }}"><i class="fas fa-chevron-left text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i></c-buttons.secondary>
            {% else %}
                <c-buttons.secondary size="sm" aria-label="Previous page" disabled><i class="fas fa-chevron-left text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i></c-buttons.secondary>
            {% endif %}
            <span class="text-sm text-text-muted">Page {{ vuln_panel.page }} / {{ vuln_panel.page_count }}</span>
            {% if vuln_panel.has_next %}
                <c-buttons.secondary size="sm" aria-label="Next page" href="{{ vuln_next_url }}"><i class="fas fa-chevron-right text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i></c-buttons.secondary>
            {% else %}
                <c-buttons.secondary size="sm" aria-label="Next page" disabled><i class="fas fa-chevron-right text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i></c-buttons.secondary>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    {% endif %}
    </c-tables.footer>
    </c-tables.shell>
</div>
